--- a/data/org.mate.panel.toplevel.gschema.xml.in
+++ b/data/org.mate.panel.toplevel.gschema.xml.in
@@ -70,6 +70,11 @@
       <summary>Float the panel off the screen edge</summary>
       <description>If true, the panel stands off the edge of the screen it is at, with rounded corners, and the space it reserves counts the gap. This is only done under Caminito, the Wayland compositor, and is ignored anywhere else.</description>
     </key>
+    <key name="intellihide" type="b">
+      <default>false</default>
+      <summary>Hide the panel while a window overlaps it</summary>
+      <description>If true, the panel reserves no space and asks Caminito, the Wayland compositor, to hide it while a window on its output's active workspace overlaps it, and to show it again when none does or when the pointer rests at its edge. The key does nothing under any other compositor or on X11.</description>
+    </key>
